{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e5a2f2b0-9b1a-4b3e-8b7a-exam-service-1",
    "name": "Exam Service",
    "description": "Covers courses, exams, the full exam-attempt lifecycle (start -> answer -> finalize/grade -> cancel) and academic-record wiring for the Exam Service (see cpr/PAD-team1/exam-service/README.md section 8 for the auth/role table this mirrors).\n\nThis collection mints its own JWTs via the collection-level pre-request script (HS256, signed with the same dev secrets as config/dev.exs), and every run generates fresh, non-colliding course/exam/player ids, so importing it and clicking \"Run\" is enough — no manual token-pasting or id edits needed.\n\nFolders 1-3 are safe to run automatically end-to-end. Folder 4 (the 410 expired-attempt case) is deliberately excluded from an automatic run — the attempt window is a real 10 minutes server-side, so it needs a manual wait; see its own description. The ExUnit suite already covers that case deterministically.\n\nIf your local dev secrets differ from the defaults (config/dev.exs's jwt_secret / service_jwt_secret), update the `jwt_secret` / `service_jwt_secret` collection variables before running.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Stable per-run identifiers: generated once per collection run, reused by every",
          "// request within that run, so re-running the whole collection never collides with",
          "// data from a previous run.",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get(\"run_id\")) {",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"run_id\", Date.now().toString());",
          "}",
          "const runId = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"run_id\");",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"course_id\", \"postman-course-\" + runId);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"player_id\", \"postman-player-\" + runId);",
          "",
          "// Minimal HS256 JWT signer using Postman's bundled CryptoJS — lets this collection",
          "// mint its own valid player/moderator/service tokens instead of needing them pasted",
          "// in by hand before every run.",
          "function base64url(wordArray) {",
          "    return CryptoJS.enc.Base64.stringify(wordArray)",
          "        .replace(/\\+/g, \"-\")",
          "        .replace(/\\//g, \"_\")",
          "        .replace(/=+$/, \"\");",
          "}",
          "",
          "function signJWT(payload, secret) {",
          "    const header = { alg: \"HS256\", typ: \"JWT\" };",
          "    const encodedHeader = base64url(CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.parse(JSON.stringify(header)));",
          "    const encodedPayload = base64url(CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.parse(JSON.stringify(payload)));",
          "    const signingInput = encodedHeader + \".\" + encodedPayload;",
          "    const signature = base64url(CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(signingInput, secret));",
          "    return signingInput + \".\" + signature;",
          "}",
          "",
          "const jwtSecret = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"jwt_secret\");",
          "const serviceSecret = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"service_jwt_secret\");",
          "",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(",
          "    \"player_token\",",
          "    signJWT({ sub: pm.collectionVariables.get(\"player_id\"), roles: [\"player\"] }, jwtSecret)",
          ");",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(",
          "    \"moderator_token\",",
          "    signJWT({ sub: \"postman-mod-\" + runId, roles: [\"player\", \"moderator\"] }, jwtSecret)",
          ");",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(",
          "    \"service_token\",",
          "    signJWT({ roles: [\"service\"] }, serviceSecret)",
          ");"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:4000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "jwt_secret", "value": "dev_only_jwt_secret_do_not_use_in_prod", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "service_jwt_secret", "value": "dev_only_service_jwt_secret_do_not_use_in_prod", "type": "string" },
